  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Upstream</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Upstream will empower 100 marginalized youth (16-25). In Isingiro District with skills to build sustainable livelihoods. Over 14 months, the initiative will enhance youth employability through agribusiness, environmental sustainability, and entrepreneurship training.The program will enroll two cohorts of 50 participants, providing hands-on training in business development, financial literacy,and market access. In collaboration with the local government, Upstream will recruit 10 experienced mentors to coach and guide beneficiaries, ensuring personalized support.

Participants will enroll into a three-month training, covering personal effectiveness, disciplined entrepreneurship, and environmental-based social entrepreneurship. At the same time the program will implement Pop-up Hubsto foster collaboration and networking. After training, participants will refine their business ideas, develop business models, andcreate prototypes. They also will receive guidance on compliance, record-keeping, and talent management.

Each cohort will join theTayinu revolving capital fund for financial literacy, funding access, and capacity building. The 20 most promising businesses will attend the Innovation Hub in Mbarara for a three-day exchange program, connecting with business leaders and pitching for startup seed funding of up to &#x20ac;200. Selected entrepreneurs will receive tablets for virtual learning to expand their market and access resources.</narrative>
  </description>
