  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ability Youth Initiative (Tayinu) is a youth-led, youth-focused organization committed to transforming the lives of marginalized youth who have dropped out of formal education. Since 2022, we have worked directly with these young people, not just as beneficiaries but as active participants in shaping their own futures.

Our mentorship model ensures meaningful inclusion in which youth fromeconomically and socially disenfranchised backgrounds are given priority, enrolling in a year-long mentorship program before becoming full members of our general assembly. Through Tayinu&#x2019;s University Students Experiential Learning (USEL) program, we build their capacity, equipping them with skills to integrate into leadership and employment.

We believe in inclusive governance, with a five-member board that reserves a seat for youth representation. Our programs are designed through a participatory, design-thinking approach, ensuring that young people are at the heart of every decision. Tayinu applies the World Bank Group Poverty Index, evaluating income, education, household conditions, disability, and access to essential services. This data-driven approach allows us to identify those most at risk and provide tailored interventions that create real, lasting change.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ability Youth Initiative</narrative>
